.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.TH CRIMLAB 1 2026-11-12 crimlab "User Commands"
.SH NAME
crimlab \- criminology and sociolegal statistics from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crimlab
.I fn
.RB [ \-j ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\- \fIarg\fR
.IR value " ...]"
.br
.B crimlab
.BR \-l " | " \-h " | " \-V
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B crimlab
runs the function
.I fn
of the crimlab package (the name of the R function, such as
.BR orrisk )
and prints its result as a table, or as JSON with
.BR \-j .
The functions, their arguments and their checks are those of the R and
Python packages.
.PP
The arguments come from
.I file
.RB ( \-
for standard input), a JSON object of named arguments or a CSV table whose
columns are arguments, and from
.B \-\-\fIarg value\fR
options, which win. Without
.BR \-f ,
the arguments the options leave out are read from standard input.
A
.I value
is JSON when it starts with
.BR [ ", " { " or " \(dq ,
a list when it holds a comma, else one number,
.BR true ", " false ", " NA
or text. A JSON object given for a per-group argument names the groups;
a CSV column named
.B group
does the same for the other columns. Trailing empty cells of a CSV column
are dropped, and a column of one value is one value.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-j
print the result as JSON: a data frame is an object of columns, a named
vector an object of numbers, a missing value null, and a number JSON
cannot hold the string NaN, Inf or \-Inf.
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
read the arguments from
.IR file .
.TP
.B \-l
list the functions and their arguments (optional ones in brackets).
.TP
.B \-h
print a short help.
.TP
.B \-V
print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the function refuses its arguments (the message goes
to standard error), 2 for a usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
crimlab orrisk \-\-or 2 \-\-rate 0.1 \-\-share 0.3
echo \(aq{"done": [30, 45, 60], "open": [100, 150]}\(aq | crimlab losbnd \-j
crimlab vodtst \-f stops.csv \-\-ref b
crimlab proof \-\-fn vodtst
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/rootcoder007/crimlab
